<p class=MsoNormal>        &lt;h2&gt;Publishable brief&lt;/h2&gt;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>        &lt;p&gt;Micron is trading near the top of its
52-week range while public reporting points to tight AI-memory supply and
strong demand into mid-2026. The bull case is that Micron is still one of the
cleanest ways to express AI infrastructure demand, with management saying
memory shortages may last beyond 2026 and investor materials highlighting
strong recent product and manufacturing momentum. The bear case is that the
stock has already moved a long way and now needs near-perfect execution to justify
further upside, especially with earnings on June 24, 2026 and insider selling
reported earlier in May. The next report will show whether the market is still
underestimating the duration of the memory cycle or whether expectations have
gotten too far ahead of fundamentals.&lt;/p&gt;</p>

<p class=MsoNormal>      &lt;/section&gt;</p>

